questions.answer:
Three forces act on the car:

- its **weight** $F_w=mg$, vertically downward;
- the **normal force** $N$ from the track, perpendicular to the surface of the track (tilted $30^\circ$ from the vertical, towards the centre of the circle);
- the **force of friction** $F_{\text{fric}}$, acting down the slope along the surface (since the car is at its *maximum* speed, it is on the verge of sliding up and outwards, so friction acts down the incline towards the centre).

The **net force** is the centripetal force $F_c$, which is **horizontal**, directed towards the centre of the circular path.
